codex
The first symbolic attempt exposed a proof-shape issue, not an implementation issue: an ellipsis in the `<k>` cell made the continuation universally symbolic, so the prover explored unrelated continuations (including `min`) and hit a known unsupported Haskell float hook. I’m tightening the claim to an exact continuation and explicitly accounting for the function binding left by module loading.
apply patch
